        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T00:27:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The plan was to use this to implement one-device-per-adapter in Blink.\n\nHowever I\u0027m realizing now that this won\u0027t work, because we aren\u0027t supposed to consume the adapter unless requestDevice succeeds. But Blink can\u0027t know whether it succeeds until it gets called back.\n\nInstead I think we need an extension to DeviceDescriptor that tells dawn to consume the adapter.",
      "parentUuid": "accd6fcc_8a6945fb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "41426f5cefb766fa584c64ae2e84e1e06055087e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33ec5d32_309daf2c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/dawn.json",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T01:23:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couldn\u0027t Blink just ensure that `MultipleDevicesPerAdapter` is enabled on the instance it creates then? Or is this for like a migration/transition thing?",
      "parentUuid": "643da13c_c99f4be5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "41426f5cefb766fa584c64ae2e84e1e06055087e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf9cc5bf_7dbd160b",
        "filename": "src/dawn/dawn.json",
        "patchSetId": 30
      },
      "lineNbr": 134,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T01:49:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Blink would need MultipleDevicesPerAdapter to be disabled, but other parts of Chromium need it to enabled (currently - I\u0027m not sure how hard of a requirement this is).\n\nI don\u0027t think we can have multiple instances because all the parts of Chromium have to interoperate.",
      "parentUuid": "33ec5d32_309daf2c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "41426f5cefb766fa584c64ae2e84e1e06055087e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
